From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 01:52:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] control: remap - pass unmapped name ids to the child

Since commit 166407da ("control: remap - fix numid lookup issue"),
remap_find_numid_app returns NULL for numid 0. An element id given by
name only (numid 0) that matches no remap entry, the way
"amixer cset name=..." addresses a control, therefore reaches
remap_load_list and then fails with -ENOENT, so no element that the
remap passes through can be read or written by name. Before that
commit numid 0 was passed to the child unchanged.

The remap is the default control device of every card whose UCM
configuration merges controls (for example the WSA88xx two-speaker
"Speakers Volume"), as soon as alsactl has saved it, so name based
amixer access to all other controls of those cards fails.

Pass a name based id that matches no remap entry to the child as is,
which resolves the name, and only translate the numid back to the
application numid when one was set.

Fixes: 166407da ("control: remap - fix numid lookup issue")
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/control/control_remap.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/control/control_remap.c b/src/control/control_remap.c
index 80a0f43b..14de1628 100644
--- a/src/control/control_remap.c
+++ b/src/control/control_remap.c
@@ -309,7 +309,7 @@ _retry:
 			}
 		}
 		*id = rid->id_child;
-	} else {
+	} else if (id->numid > 0) {
 		numid = remap_find_numid_app(priv, id->numid);
 		if (numid) {
 			id->numid = numid->numid_child;
@@ -343,7 +343,7 @@ static int remap_id_to_app(snd_ctl_remap_t *priv, snd_ctl_elem_id_t *id, snd_ctl
 		}
 		*id = rid->id_app;
 	} else {
-		if (err >= 0) {
+		if (err >= 0 && id->numid > 0) {
 			numid = remap_find_numid_child(priv, id->numid);
 			if (numid == NULL)
 				return -EIO;
-- 
